<!-- The front node of the full stack (conf/full-stack/README.md; plans/Edge-Node2.md §3, §4.7): the front option set
    alone (node_role front) before an edge cluster, whose members pair with it once and each dial it, as one pairing
    and its pool. It is conf/front/MoquiFrontConf.xml, whose comments say what each setting does; this one says what the
    full stack adds. Nothing of it is set here by hand: the names and the link names come from the edge members, and the
    mail port is a row.
    - The sites. Each edge member gives the front its mr-pass sites' hosts (and its chat address's host) as terminate
      hosts, so the front ends their TLS, sees the session cookie and balances them over the live members, sticky by it.
      With front_edge members, every name of their local nodes too, each in its own mode, which the member forwards
      down that node's link; with edge members a local node gives its names to the front itself, by a second pairing.
    - The edge members' link names. Each member names its own edge_link_url in its Hello; the front keeps the host as
      a link name of that member (Edge Clients › Domains) and passes its connections through untouched to that member
      alone, picked by the server name before the link's ALPN, so a local node's link reaches the member as if dialed
      directly. A link name is never balanced: while its member is not linked its connections are refused.
    - Mail. Port 25 as an EdgePort row of kind smtp for the edge cluster's pairing (System › Edge Clients › Ports):
      each connection goes to a live member's SMTP listener with a PROXY header naming the client, which makes every
      check itself. MX records name the front.
    - Not here: call media, TURN and SIP are at each edge member's own address. XMPP and SSH ports stay the edge
      members' own with front_edge members; with edge members, which bind none, the front's ports take each local
      node's domain by its front pairing.
    Build and run as conf/front: Maximal (embedded Postgres is enough), the base components only. -->
<moqui-conf xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/moqui-conf-3.xsd">
    <default-property name="instance_purpose" value="production"/>
    <default-property name="node_role" value="front"/>
    <!-- before anything goes to an edge member; a ban an edge member starts is told up its front link, and the front
        refuses that client for the pairing's names. A ban is not told on: one a local node starts reaches its own edge
        members (and the front only by its own front pairing, with edge members), not the front through them. Every local node behind front_edge members is part of the edge
        cluster's one pairing here, so a ban, a rule and a limit per pairing holds for the edge cluster as a whole. -->
    <default-property name="webapp_web_protection" value="true"/>

    <!-- .env: webapp_http_host, the front's own name (where the edge members pair, and its System app), with a WebPKI
        certificate in runtime/cert; edge_public_addresses, its public addresses; edge_link_key and the other secrets
        made at the first start. The sites' certificates are here, as terminate hosts: in runtime/cert, or System ›
        Certificates with ACME. A passthrough name's certificate and each link name's are on the node that ends its
        TLS, whose ACME challenge passes through. -->

    <!-- Backups: the pairing, host names, the mail port and the certificates are rows (conf/front/MoquiFrontConf.xml). -->
    <default-property name="embedded_db_backup_scheduled" value="true"/>

    <entity-facade crypt-pass="${entity_ds_crypt_pass}" query-stats="true"/>

    <!-- Balancing the edge members: the sites' requests by the session cookie, the mail port and passthrough names by
        the client's address. An edge member set aside after failures gets no new work for a while, and one drained on
        the front's Edge Clients › Clients (Members, Drain) gets none until it resumes, for its rolling upgrade. -->
    <edge sticky-cookie="moqui.session" set-aside-failures="3" set-aside-seconds="30"/>
</moqui-conf>
